# Normalize text files to LF in the repository regardless of which OS checked them in or
# out — this codebase is edited from both Linux/Mac (LF) and Windows/WAMP (CRLF often
# introduced by editors/tools that default to it), and without this, a save-and-commit from
# either side turns into a full-file diff of nothing but line-ending noise, burying the real
# change (this is exactly what happened once already — see the "production tree sync" commit).
# Git still checks files out using each platform's native line ending if core.autocrlf is set
# there; only what's stored in the repo (and diffed) is normalized.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.sqlite binary
